Subject: Require pinned pthread headers and expand actual C/Rust ABI records

Reproduced old mainline SDK missing pthread_condattr_t.cond_clock. Reject it
before std compilation; private composition uses the pinned pthread2 headers.
Compare file metadata, clocks, exact pthread attributes/once, and the capacity
and alignment (not array stride compatibility) of opaque synchronization storage.
Native ino_t is the SDK __ino_t, publicly gated by feature macros.
Base: preceding patches on PR1800 2eb81b4. APL 1.1; original John KNIPPER,
adaptations copyright AROS contributors. Runtime remains UNTESTED.

--- a/tools/crosstools/rust/unmodified/profiles.py
+++ b/tools/crosstools/rust/unmodified/profiles.py
@@ -19,6 +19,11 @@
     config = sdk / "include/aros/config.h"
     if not config.is_file() or "#define AROS_DOS_PACKETS                1" not in config.read_text():
         raise ValueError("require native mainline ABIv1 SDK configuration, not ABIv11")
+
+    pthread = sdk / "include/pthread.h"
+    import re
+    if not pthread.is_file() or not re.search(r"\bclockid_t\s+cond_clock\s*;", pthread.read_text(errors='replace')):
+        raise ValueError("require the pinned pthread2 headers with cond_clock; older mainline SDK is not this profile")
 
 
